   "text": "```yaml\n- id: DR-01\n  requirement: >\n    The service must hold a shared picture of the airspace that includes the network of flight corridors between sites, the zones that group those corridors, and the closures announced by the authorities.\n- id: DR-02\n  requirement: >\n    The service must record each closure as either planned, with a start time and an end time, or sudden, applying immediately on entry.\n- id: DR-03\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let the airspace desk amend an existing closure, including widening its area and moving its end time, and must record when each amendment was made.\n- id: DR-04\n  requirement: >\n    The service must update the shared picture when a closure is entered or amended during the day, not only when it is first entered.\n- id: DR-05\n  requirement: >\n    The service must make a closure that comes into force, or is amended, while drones are airborne visible to the dispatcher responsible for each affected flight at the time of the change.\n- id: DR-06\n  requirement: >\n    The service must not choose a drone, choose a route, or sign off a flight on a dispatcher's behalf; the responsible dispatcher must make and sign off each of these decisions.\n- id: DR-07\n  requirement: >\n    The service must record, for each flight plan, the drone, the route, and the dispatcher who is responsible for the flight.\n- id: DR-08\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow a dispatcher to call off a flight.\n- id: DR-09\n  requirement: >\n    The service must allow several dispatchers to plan flights at the same time for the same sites and the same drones without one dispatcher's change silently overwriting another's.\n- id: DR-10\n  requirement: >\n    The service must show the airspace desk, when a closure is entered, a measure of how much disruption that closure caused across all customer companies; the definition of \"disruption\" must be agreed with the airspace desk before this measure is built.\n- id: DR-11\n  requirement: >\n    The service must not show the airspace desk the operational details of any single customer company; cross-customer disruption must be shown only in aggregate.\n- id: DR-12\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a technician add a drone to the fleet and retire a drone from the fleet.\n- id: DR-13\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a technician record each drone's status as in service, out of service for repair, or sent to charge, and must let the technician change that status, including returning a drone to service.\n- id: DR-14\n  requirement: >\n    The service must let a technician add and record charging pads at each site.\n```"
